    "5b81e53c-9eaf-4cb4-b198-392f3328f6b4": {
      "id": "5b81e53c-9eaf-4cb4-b198-392f3328f6b4",
      "message": {
        "id": "5b81e53c-9eaf-4cb4-b198-392f3328f6b4",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1773423090.661218,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "If you’re asking **“What was the human lifespan in the 1st century?”**, historians and archaeologists estimate it roughly like this:\n\n### Average life expectancy\nIn the **1st century CE** (during the time of the entity[\"historical_period\",\"Roman Empire\"] and the life of entity[\"people\",\"Jesus Christ\"]):\n\n- **Average life expectancy at birth:** about **25–35 years**.\n\nBut this number is **misleading**.\n\n### Why it was so low\nMany people died **very young**, which pulled the average down:\n\n- High **infant mortality** (many children died before age 5)\n- **Diseases** with no antibiotics\n- **Infections and injuries**\n- **Poor sanitation**\n- **War and famine**\n\n### If someone survived childhood\nIf a person made it past childhood (around age 10–15), they often lived much longer:\n\n- Typical adult lifespan: **50–60 years**\n- Some lived **70+ years**\n\nThere are records of people even reaching **80 years**.\n\n### Example from historical sources\nAncient Roman records show:\n\n- Soldiers often served until **40–50**\n- Philosophers and politicians sometimes lived **60–70**\n\n### Comparison with today\nToday in countries like entity[\"country\",\"Canada\"]:\n\n- Average life expectancy is about **81–82 years**\n\n### Simple way to understand it\nThink of 100 babies born in the 1st century:\n\n- Many died before age **5**\n- Those who survived often lived to **50–60**\n\nSo people **weren’t dying at 30** normally — the average is low because many **children died early**.\n\n---\n\nIf you want, I can also explain something interesting:  \n**How ancient texts like the entity[\"book\",\"Bible\"] describe people living 100–900 years and what historians think about that.** It’s a fascinating topic."
          ]
